ses (direct or indirect) that are equivalent to OMIMs - the subclasses should (not must) have a logical def that uses the PS as a genus (see http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/patterns/disease_series_by_gene.yaml) - the OMIM subclasses must have acronym synonyms that are the parent syn + number, e.g. HPE1, HPE2 - the primary label for the children should also be parent + {\"type\"} + number - the first member will usually have the same number local ID as the PS - the first member in OMIM usually has documentation that is pertinent to the parent PS - the members may(?) generally share high semantic similarity - All OMIMPS disease should have a has characteristic some inherited restricted, see http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/sparql/omimps-should-be-inherited-violation.sparql\n\n  Line 657: | IRI | http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/patterns/disease_series_by_gene.yaml |\n\n  Line 658: | Name | disease_series_by_gene |\n\n  Line 670: | IRI | http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/patterns/disease_series_by_gene.yaml |\n\n  Line 671: | Name | disease_series_by_gene_and_inheritance |\n\n  Line 675: | Examples | [mondo](https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/blob/master/src/patterns/data/matches/disease_series_by_gene_and_inheritance.tsv) |\n\n  Line 686: See full table [here](https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/blob/master/src/patterns/data/matches/disease_series_by_gene_and_inheritance.tsv)\n\n  Line 1485: | IRI | http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/patterns/nonhuman_disease_series_by_gene.yaml |\n\n  Line 1486: | Name | nonhuman_disease_series_by_gene |\n\n\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/src/patterns/dosdp-patterns/OMIM_phenotypic_series.yaml:\n  Line 13:   (see http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/patterns/disease_series_by_gene.yaml)\n\n\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/src/patterns/dosdp-patterns/OMIM_disease_series_by_gene.yaml:\n  Line 1: pattern_name: OMIM_disease_series_by_gene\n\n  L